**What pressing a row's button does: never posts - it opens a window**, chosen by the action's slot 15 token, placed at the `.gui` position `diplo_request_pos`, added to the idler (CEU3Idler::AddDialog) and kept at view +0x518:
- 0x2F5 declarewar (and limited war, the same class) and 0x7A4 add_war_goal -> **CWarGoalDialog** (0xA8 bytes);
- 0x6DA trade_action -> **CTradeDiplomacyDialog** (0xB0);
- 0x71A send_expedition -> **CExpeditionaryForceDialog** (0x12C);
- 0x71C licence_technology -> **CLicenceTechnologyDialog** (0x138);
- 0x75D share_technology -> **CShareTechnologyDialog** (0x78) when value is set, else the standard one;
- 0x2F7 alliance, 0x2FC guarantee, 0x2FE milaccess, 0x2FF offermilaccess, 0x309 callaction, 0x4A1 influence, 0x6CD nap, 0x6D0 influence_leaders, 0x6D3 embargo, 0x6D4 faction_action, 0x726 debt, 0x729 peace, 0x804 request_lendlease, 0x844 offer_lendlease -> **CStandadDiplomacyDialogue** (0x74), the `DefaultDiplomacyDialog` of diplomacydialog.gui;
- 0x2F8 also opens the standard one, but no class answers that token (dead);
- any other token: nothing.
Two bare `ret`s, 0x78BDE0 and 0x78BEEE.
